'' =============================================================================
''  test-F260-input  --  does the Goertzel summer read its ADC pin AT ALL?
'' =============================================================================
''  WHY A SECOND, SMALLER PROBE
''  test-f260-goertzel.spin2 grew across 23 rounds to 1,640 lines and 214
''  debug() sites. Spin2 DEBUG() statements resolve to unique BRK #1..255
''  instructions (Spin2 v55 doc), so that probe was near the ceiling -- and its
''  last run came back as a debugger memory dump instead of output. Most of its
''  arms answer questions that are now CLOSED and recorded in the findings
''  register and in git; carrying them costs debug slots, run time and log
''  legibility. This probe carries only the open question.
''
''  WHAT IS ALREADY SETTLED (do not re-test here):
''    the analog loopback works, DC, repeatedly (C5: ~1,635 high / ~336 low)
''    the streamer DAC override drives from a launched cog when the pin names
''      that cog in M[3:0] -- Chip's `setnib dacmode,cogid,#2` idiom (C10:
''      1,640 vs 332)
''    pppp*4 = base pin; S[15:12] = sum-select; S[19:16] = invert-select
''    the NCO scale is 2^31; DAC output inverts each LUT byte's MSB
''    the accumulators carry a large offset by design -- Chip's demo calibrates
''      it out
''    sum-select, block-select and all five documented ADC setups are FLAT
''      against a real tone
''
''  THE OPEN QUESTION
''  Eight rounds tested with a TONE. DC is far more robust: if the summer reads
''  the pin at all, holding it HIGH vs LOW makes the bitstream sum m
''  predominantly +1 vs -1, and the accumulators must move a long way. No
''  frequency match, no phase alignment, no correlation subtleties to get wrong.
''  A flat result here means the input path is dead and no tone test could ever
''  have worked.
''
''  Build: pnut-ts -d test-f260-goertzel-input.spin2
''  Rig:   jumper pin 0 -> pin 1. Unchanged.
'' =============================================================================

CON
  _clkfreq  = 200_000_000
  BUILD     = 5

  '' BUILD 4 RESULT -- the duration control PASSED (20,009 at 1 MHz vs 10,009
  '' at 2 MHz), so the detector really is being swept and the flat reading is
  '' not a parameter that failed to arrive. But it exposed a contradiction
  '' INSIDE THIS PROBE:
  ''     DC section, pin driven, S_BASE1, detector 1 MHz : cos ~112
  ''     TONE tag 0, pin driven LOW by the same pinclear+pinl, same S_BASE1,
  ''       same command, same detector                    : cos ~1,057,440
  '' Same pin state, same parameters, four orders of magnitude apart. One of
  '' those readings is lying, and until I know which, NEITHER the DC conclusion
  '' ("the summer reads the pin") nor the tone conclusion ("no selectivity") is
  '' safe. So BUILD 5 runs the two code paths back to back on identical
  '' configurations and prints both. If the repeat matches the DC section, the
  '' difference is something in the tone path; if it matches the tone section,
  '' the difference is HISTORY -- state left behind by whatever ran earlier --
  '' and every arm in this probe is order-dependent.

  '' BUILD 3 RESULT: on-target 1,058,407 / detuned 1,059,491 / tone-off
  '' 1,059,658 -- all within 0.1%. No selectivity. But two faults were MINE:
  ''   1. "tone off" FLOATED the pin. A floating input is a noise source, not
  ''      a null. The DC test already showed a DRIVEN static level integrates
  ''      to near nothing -- that is the real null.
  ''   2. I printed only the QVECTOR magnitude. The DC arms show cos in the
  ''      hundreds while the tone arms show magnitude near 1,059,000, and I
  ''      cannot reconcile those without the raw accumulators.
  '' BUILD 4 prints cos, sin and the WAITXFI duration for every tone arm --
  '' duration is the control that proves the detector frequency actually
  '' changed (100 cycles at 2 MHz must take half as long as at 1 MHz) -- and
  '' nulls by driving the pin low instead of floating it.

  '' BUILD 2 RESULT -- the debugger was the confound.
  ''   no crash; the launched cogs' "CogN INIT" lines vanished, confirming
  ''   DEBUG_COGS took effect
  ''   accumulators collapsed from ~1,000,000-7,000,000 to 0/350/-86/168/422,
  ''   so those millions were debug-interrupt damage, NOT the by-design offset
  ''   I attributed them to
  ''   S=0 gave delta 0,0 EXACTLY -- the sum-select control works for the first
  ''   time
  ''   base+1 (the ADC pin) moved 563/-277 while base+0/2/3 all sat on the same
  ''   fixed artifact (-127/-3), so THE SUMMER READS THE PIN
  ''
  '' Note the DC test could only ever answer "is the pin connected to the
  '' summer": Goertzel REJECTS DC by construction, integrating a static input to
  '' near zero over whole NCO cycles, so a small delta there is correct.
  '' The real question needs a TONE -- and every tone null this campaign was
  '' taken with the debug interrupt live in the streaming cog.

  '' THE DEBUGGER WAS IN THE STREAMER'S COG THE WHOLE TIME.
  '' p2kbArchDebugInterrupt, limitations:
  ''     streamer_interaction: "Debug can disrupt streamer operations."
  ''     workaround:           "Disable debug when using streamer."
  '' DEBUG_COGS defaults to %11111111 -- EVERY cog has debug capability enabled
  '' at runtime -- and the "CogN INIT ..." lines in every log this campaign are
  '' the debugger announcing cog starts, i.e. proof it was live in the launched
  '' engine cogs. Every streamer measurement we have taken was made with the
  '' highest-priority interrupt in the P2 enabled inside the cog running the
  '' streamer, in a probe that is entirely about the streamer.
  '' Restrict it to cog 0, which is the only cog that reports.
  DEBUG_COGS = %0000_0001

  DAC_PIN   = 0
  ADC_PIN   = 1

  CYCLES    = 100
  NCO_Y_1M  = 21_474_836                 ' 2^32 * 1 MHz / 200 MHz, X=1
  TONE_HZ   = 1_000_000
  SAMPLES   = 2000

  X_DDS_G_SINC1 = $F007_0000             ' verified: Spin2 v55 symbol table
  DDS_D     = X_DDS_G_SINC1 | CYCLES     ' block base 0 (pins 0..3), no DAC out
  S_BASE0   = %0001 << 12                ' sum base+0 = pin 0
  S_BASE1   = %0010 << 12                ' sum base+1 = pin 1, our ADC pin
  S_BASE2   = %0100 << 12
  S_BASE3   = %1000 << 12
  S_NONE    = 0

  MODE_GTZL = 0
  MODE_COUNT = 1

VAR
  long g[16]
  '  [0] dds_d  [1] dds_s  [2] mode
  '  [0] dds_d [1] dds_s [2] mode [3] detector Hz
  '  [8] cos [9] sin [10] density [11] waitxfi [12] magnitude [15] done


PUB main() | hi, lo

  debug("=== F-260 input probe, BUILD ", udec_(BUILD), " ===")

  if not continuity()
    debug("*** no jumper on pin 0 -> pin 1. STOP.")
    halt()

  '' ---- C5: prove the analog path, DC, before asking anything else --------
  hi := level_density(1)
  lo := level_density(0)
  debug("C5 analog path : pin high -> ", udec_(hi), "   low -> ", udec_(lo), "   spread ", udec_(hi - lo))
  if (hi - lo) < 200
    debug("*** C5 FAILED: the ADC pin does not see the driven level. Nothing")
    debug("*** below can mean anything. STOP.")
    halt()
  debug("   the ADC pin's raw bitstream tracks the driven level.")

  '' ---- DC: does the summer respond to that same static input? -----------
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- DC response, by sum-select ---")
  dc_pair(S_BASE0, 0)
  dc_pair(S_BASE1, 1)
  dc_pair(S_BASE2, 2)
  dc_pair(S_BASE3, 3)
  dc_pair(S_NONE, 9)
  debug(" ")
  tone_arms()
  halt()


'' --- the real test: an independent tone, detector swept ---------------------
'' A smart-pin NCO on the DAC pin makes a real 1 MHz square wave from cog 0,
'' independent of the streamer and of any cog's DAC channels. The detector is
'' then swept against it. This is the first time this comparison has been made
'' with the debug interrupt OUT of the streaming cog.
PRI tone_arms() | on_t, off_t, null_t
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- TONE: independent smart-pin NCO on pin 0, detector swept ---")
  tone_on()
  on_t  := tone_row(TONE_HZ, 1)
  off_t := tone_row(TONE_HZ * 2, 2)
  tone_off()
  null_t := tone_row(TONE_HZ, 0)

  '' Same configuration as the DC section, run again HERE, late in the
  '' sequence. This is the discriminator: path or history?
  debug(" ")
  debug("--- REPEAT of the DC configuration, run late ---")
  drive(1)
  gtzl(S_BASE1)
  debug("  pin HIGH via the DC path : waitxfi=", udec_(g[11]), "  cos=", sdec_(g[8]), " sin=", sdec_(g[9]))
  drive(0)
  gtzl(S_BASE1)
  debug("  pin LOW  via the DC path : waitxfi=", udec_(g[11]), "  cos=", sdec_(g[8]), " sin=", sdec_(g[9]))
  float_pin()
  debug("  DC section reported cos in the HUNDREDS for this configuration.")
  debug("  Matching that here => the tone path differs. Matching the tone")
  debug("  rows (~1,000,000) => the probe is ORDER-DEPENDENT and every")
  debug("  earlier reading in it is suspect.")
  debug(" ")
  if on_t > (null_t * 4) and on_t > (off_t * 4)
    debug("GOERTZEL DETECTS. On-target beats both the detuned detector and the")
    debug("tone-off null, against a source the detector shares no NCO with.")
    debug("The mode works. The guide's TEXT is the whole defect -- and the")
    debug("debug interrupt in the streaming cog was what hid it for 23 rounds.")
  else
    debug("Still no selective detection, but now with a CLEAN streamer cog.")
    debug("That is a very different claim from the earlier nulls, and it is")
    debug("the one worth putting to Chip.")


'' One tone measurement, printing the raw accumulators and the run duration.
'' Duration is the control that the detector frequency really changed: 100
'' cycles at 2 MHz must take half the clocks of 100 cycles at 1 MHz.
PRI tone_row(detector_hz, tag) : mag
  run_at(DDS_D, S_BASE1, MODE_GTZL, detector_hz)
  mag := g[12]
  debug("  tag ", udec_(tag), "  detector ", udec_(detector_hz / 1000), " kHz   waitxfi=", udec_(g[11]), "   cos=", sdec_(g[8]), " sin=", sdec_(g[9]), "  mag=", udec_(mag))


PRI gtzl_mag(detector_hz) : mag
  run_at(DDS_D, S_BASE1, MODE_GTZL, detector_hz)
  mag := g[12]


PRI tone_on()
  pinclear(DAC_PIN)
  wrpin(DAC_PIN, P_NCO_FREQ | P_OE)
  wxpin(DAC_PIN, 1)
  pinhigh(DAC_PIN)                         ' enable FIRST, then set frequency
  wypin(DAC_PIN, NCO_Y_1M)
  waitms(5)


'' A real null: the pin DRIVEN to a static level. Floating it would leave the
'' ADC on an undriven input, which is a noise source, not a null.
PRI tone_off()
  pinclear(DAC_PIN)
  pinl(DAC_PIN)
  waitms(5)


PRI dc_pair(ssel, label) | hi_c, hi_s, lo_c, lo_s
  drive(1)
  gtzl(ssel)
  hi_c := g[8]
  hi_s := g[9]
  drive(0)
  gtzl(ssel)
  lo_c := g[8]
  lo_s := g[9]
  float_pin()
  debug("  sum base+", udec_(label), "  delta cos=", sdec_(hi_c - lo_c), "  delta sin=", sdec_(hi_s - lo_s), "   (high cos=", sdec_(hi_c), ")")


'' Hold the DAC pin at a hard digital level from cog 0 and leave it held.
PRI drive(high)
  pinclear(DAC_PIN)
  if high
    pinh(DAC_PIN)
  else
    pinl(DAC_PIN)
  waitms(5)


PRI float_pin()
  pinf(DAC_PIN)


PRI continuity() : ok | hi, lo
  pinclear(DAC_PIN)
  pinclear(ADC_PIN)
  pinf(ADC_PIN)
  pinh(DAC_PIN)
  waitms(2)
  hi := pinr(ADC_PIN)
  pinl(DAC_PIN)
  waitms(2)
  lo := pinr(ADC_PIN)
  pinf(DAC_PIN)
  ok := (hi == 1) and (lo == 0)


'' Count one-bits in the ADC pin's raw bitstream while cog 0 holds a level.
PRI level_density(high) : bits
  drive(high)
  run(0, 0, MODE_COUNT)
  float_pin()
  bits := g[10]


PRI gtzl(ssel)
  run(DDS_D, ssel, MODE_GTZL)


PRI run(ddsd, ssel, mode) | cogn, t0
  run_at(ddsd, ssel, mode, TONE_HZ)


PRI run_at(ddsd, ssel, mode, detector_hz) | cogn, t0
  longfill(@g[0], 0, 16)
  g[0] := ddsd
  g[1] := ssel
  g[2] := mode
  g[3] := detector_hz
  cogn := coginit(NEWCOG, @engine, @g[0])
  t0 := getct()
  repeat until g[15] == 1 or (getct() - t0) > (clkfreq / 4)
  if g[15] <> 1
    cogstop(cogn)
    debug("   *** engine did not finish")


PRI halt()
  debug(" ")
  debug("@@@ TEST COMPLETE @@@")
  repeat


'' ===========================================================================
DAT             org

engine
                mov     pb_, ptra
                mov     t_, pb_
                rdlong  ddsd_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                rdlong  ssel_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                rdlong  mode_, t_

                ' ADC pin: raw delta-sigma, no smart-pin mode, no DIR --
                ' the DDS/Goertzel section's requirement, and Chip's demo's.
                wrpin   ##P_ADC_1X, #ADC_PIN

                cmp     mode_, #MODE_COUNT      wz
        if_z    jmp     #count_arm

                ' NCO word: QFRAC gives (f<<32)/clk; the NCO masks its MSB so
                ' the scale is 2^31 -- halve it.
                mov     t_, pb_
                add     t_, #3*4
                rdlong  freq_, t_
                qfrac   freq_, ##_clkfreq
                getqx   xfrq_
                shr     xfrq_, #1

                call    #build_table
                setxfrq xfrq_

                getxacc gclr_                   ' start from cleared accs
                mov     gclr2_, 0-0             ' the mandatory follower

                getct   t0_
                xinit   ddsd_, ssel_
                mov     tq_, t0_
                add     tq_, ##20_000_000       ' 100 ms timeout
                setq    tq_
                waitxfi                         wc
                getct   t1_
                sub     t1_, t0_

                getxacc cos_                    ' cos -> D, sin -> next S
                mov     sin_, 0-0
                qvector cos_, sin_              ' D = X (cos), S = Y (sin)
                getqx   mag_
                jmp     #report

count_arm
                waitx   ##200_000
                mov     dens_, #0
                mov     tc_, ##SAMPLES
.cl             testp   #ADC_PIN                wc
        if_c    add     dens_, #1
                djnz    tc_, #.cl
                jmp     #report

'' 512-entry table: sine in byte 3, cosine in byte 2 -- the Goertzel
'' reference. Byte 0 is unused here; this probe drives no DAC.
build_table
                mov     z_, #$1FF
.bt             mov     w_, z_
                shl     w_, #32-9
                qrotate #127, w_
                getqy   sy_
                getqx   sx_
                shl     sy_, #24
                setbyte sy_, sx_, #2
                wrlut   sy_, z_                 ' register address: full 0..511
                djnf    z_, #.bt
                ret

report
                mov     t_, pb_
                add     t_, #8*4
                wrlong  cos_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                wrlong  sin_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                wrlong  dens_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                wrlong  t1_, t_
                add     t_, #4
                wrlong  mag_, t_
                mov     t_, pb_
                add     t_, #15*4
                wrlong  #1, t_                  ' done -- always the last write
                cogid   t_
                cogstop t_

pb_             res     1
t_              res     1
t0_             res     1
t1_             res     1
tq_             res     1
tc_             res     1
ddsd_           res     1
ssel_           res     1
mode_           res     1
freq_           res     1
mag_            res     1
xfrq_           res     1
cos_            res     1
sin_            res     1
dens_           res     1
gclr_           res     1
gclr2_          res     1
z_              res     1
w_              res     1
sx_             res     1
sy_             res     1
